    {
      "id": 99,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Configured telemetry flow (not auto-discovered)",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 68,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Fedora host \u2192 Agent \u2192 Gateway \u2192 destinations\n\n`fedora-worker` \u2192 **otel-hostmetrics-agent** (hostmetrics receiver, 30s) \u2192 **OTLP/gRPC :4317** \u2192 **otel-gateway** (OTLP receiver / memory limiter / transform / batch) \u2192 **Prometheus** (scrapes Gateway exporter `:8889`) **and** **Mimir** (Prometheus remote write `/api/v1/push`).\n\n**Self-monitoring (separate path):** Prometheus scrapes Agent and Gateway `:8888`. This topology describes the deployed configuration; rates and scrape health do **not** prove backend ingestion or trace an individual metric end to end.\n\n**Troubleshooting:** If an exporter panel shows \u201cNo data,\u201d check which `otelcol_exporter_*` metric names your Collector exposes before modifying the query."
      }
    },
